==========================================================================
=== CHECK: does ironwood_empty_tree_root() equal the node's empty Ironwood root?
==========================================================================
Date:    2026-10-25
Chain:   local Z3 regtest (zfnd/zebra:6.4.2, zingodevops/zainod:0.10.0-no-tls)
Method:  Zebra JSON-RPC http://127.0.0.1:8181 (basic auth zebra:zebra),
         method z_gettreestate, params ["<height>"], heights 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 112.
         Helper value read from the built napi module:
           node -e "console.log(require('./packages/core/index.js').ironwoodEmptyTreeRoot())"

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
RAW OUTPUT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
helper ironwood_empty_tree_root() = ae2935f1dfd8a24aed7c70df7de3a668eb7a49b1319880dde2bbd9031ae5d82f

chain tip = 112

height | ironwood section | ironwood finalState | ironwood finalRoot
-------|------------------|---------------------|--------------------
     0 | ABSENT           | -                   | -
     1 | ABSENT           | -                   | -
     2 | present          | 01231d487ce1194c8b2 | 73d0fc4cd8b1808df423819c9996057140d5c7572041a26835b3ad654f60d512
     3 | present          | 01231d487ce1194c8b2 | b380b71a22bafe2f587accb000ddc74f3b2e9cdfebb1233c2a974c951ddde806
     4 | present          | 01d33cbb11698bf4edb | 7b4ac0b4d204d83d2c1f5bb93d050765b33208a59c67cf8f2248b5bf7c865b1f
   112 | present          | 0127493603401bf51c4 | e3240f1baf4a47c550d3dafc5024456531bf2fb35bdb7aca7fe4971c79c8da3a

RESULT: no queried height reports an EMPTY Ironwood tree, so the node never printed an
        empty Ironwood finalRoot to compare against. The claim that the helper equals the
        node's empty Ironwood root is therefore UNVERIFIED by direct observation.

control: Zebra orchard tree at height 2 is empty -> finalState 000000, finalRoot ae2935f1dfd8a24aed7c70df7de3a668eb7a49b1319880dde2bbd9031ae5d82f
        helper output                                     = ae2935f1dfd8a24aed7c70df7de3a668eb7a49b1319880dde2bbd9031ae5d82f
        identical: true

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
INTERPRETATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Heights 0 and 1 are pre-NU6.3: z_gettreestate returns only `hash`, `height`,
  `time`, `sapling` and `orchard` keys — there is NO `ironwood` section at all.
* From height 2 (NU6.3 activation) the Ironwood tree is already non-empty at the
  first height that reports a section, because that block's coinbase carries an
  Ironwood action. Every later height grows the tree. A chain whose first
  post-activation block puts its shielded coinbase in Ironwood therefore never
  reports an empty Ironwood tree, so Zebra never prints an empty Ironwood
  finalRoot on this chain.
* The anchor check compares against the empty root only when the node reports the
  empty-tree marker (`000000`). That branch is exercised by the mocked tests
  (send.test.ts Scenarios 9 and 10); it has NOT been exercised against Zebra.
* Indirect control only: Zebra's encoding of an empty tree is visible for Orchard
  at height 2 (`finalState 000000`, `finalRoot ae2935f1...`), byte-identical to
  the helper. Both trees are MerkleHashOrchard trees of depth 32, which is why
  the values agree, but this is an argument, not a measurement of the Ironwood
  tree itself.

STATUS: unverified by direct observation; recorded in KNOWN_ISSUES.md.
